  "note": "The official PDF is headed 2026-27 requirements for the 2025-26 intake and publishes 75 unique coded rows for the Extended Major in Artificial Intelligence. The Extended Major is an add-on to an eligible base Major rather than a standalone degree. Students must complete at least 22 Extended Major credits and at least 12 single-counted credits; EMIA 4110, COMP 4211 and MATH 4432 are alternatives, as are EMIA 4990 and EMIA 4991. The EMIA 4990 path requires at least 9 elective credits, while EMIA 4991 requires at least 6. At most one course from each of COMP 1944/CTDL 1902/HUMA 1930, COMP 4462/DASC 3240, and IEDA 3250/MATH 3425 may count. ELEC 4230 remains because the intake-specific PDF lists it while noting that it was last offered in 2020-21 and deleted subsequently. These 75 rows cover only the Extended Major component and do not include or replace the selected Engineering base Major; they are exposed as a partial read-only list with totalCreditRequired=0 and must not produce a graduation-completion percentage.",
